WEBVTT

00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:03.980
Just look at this blue sky.

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:07.310
It's as though it's wishing us well.

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:09.690
What a great day to practice romance!

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:11.600
Don't drag the blue sky into this.

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:14.700
We'll be continuing our Love Lab.

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:18.420
You two will need to either participate 
or silently accept what we do here.

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:19.910
Fine, then.

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:23.840
Enomoto-senpai, your 
handkerchief is about to fall out.

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:25.230
Oh, my.

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:28.830
That's "Operation: Drop Your Handkerchief 
and Have It Picked Up," isn't it?

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:30.360
Th-This isn't...

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:32.740
Eno, you really do like
 that situation, don't you?

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:33.840
Shut up!

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.760
And quit staring at me!

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:39.060
Look over there!

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:14.510
<b>Love Lab Resumes! Or So We Thought...</b>

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:17.180
Club Advisor

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:17.180
Student Council President

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:19.570
Now, then...

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:23.520
It's time for our Love Lab, Master Riko.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:24.910
What's today's theme?

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:26.830
I thought of something wonderful.

00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:29.810
You're walking downhill when 
you drop all of your oranges,

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:31.790
then the dog you were walking escapes,

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:34.840
and you spill ice cream 
on the guy who helps you

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:35.900
for a special encounter!

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:38.300
That's too much. You're crossing 
the line into harassment.

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:44.380
I hate being patient                     Come on

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:40.620
But I've been frustrated for so long.

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:42.080
There's so much I want to do.

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:44.390
Stop dropping the subject on purpose!

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:47.470
If you shout that in front of the station, 
you'll encounter someone in no time.

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:50.740
Wh-What are you saying?

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:52.040
"I've been frustrated for so long..."

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:52.900
Don't write that down!

00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:54.980
What? Why not?

00:02:55.390 --> 00:02:57.820
So, why is Kurahashi your master?

00:02:58.060 --> 00:02:59.700
B-Because...

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:03.020
Because she's had lots 
of experience with love.

00:03:03.020 --> 00:03:06.300
Shooting through the heart of 
any boy she sets her sights on,

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:09.330
Riko-senpai has made numerous 
boys fall deeply in love with her.

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:12.800
They call her the amazing sniper of love.

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:19.130
<i>M-My lie is growing...</i>

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:20.260
Not bad.

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:23.180
A-Actually, um...

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:24.410
<i>This isn't good.</i>

00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:27.700
<i>At this rate, I'm bound to 
screw myself over eventually.</i>

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:31.750
<b>Already pretty
 screwed</b>

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:31.720
<i>I should be honest and tell them 
I always get turned down.</i>

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:32.770
<i>Okay.</i>

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:35.090
"The amazing sniper of love"?

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:36.610
Lies.

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:37.980
It's true!

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:41.940
<b>Stubborn</b>

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:41.940
<b>Vain</b>

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:40.760
<b>and</b>

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:41.940
<b>and               A Sore Loser</b>

00:03:43.850 --> 00:03:46.000
Love sniper aside,

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:48.200
why don't you try meeting people at mixers?

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:53.270
You mean a mixed chorus?

00:03:53.270 --> 00:03:56.900
No. But aren't mixers an urban legend?

00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:58.160
That's what my brother told me.

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:01.670
No, but only college students 
can participate in them.

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:03.830
<b>Isn't ready to make
 smart remarks</b>

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:05.190
No, no.

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:09.440
Kurahashi, middle school students 
have been doing them lately, right?

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:09.890
What?!

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:19.420
I had my first mixer when I 
entered elementary school!

00:04:19.420 --> 00:04:21.240
You were one funky six-year-old.

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:25.270
Are mixers a place to meet boys?

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:27.410
So we can meet different kinds of boys?

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:28.740
Well...

00:04:29.890 --> 00:04:32.220
<i>I played soccer until fifth grade.</i>

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:36.670
<i>And in a broad sense, my sixth grade 
cram school was a place to meet people.</i>

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:38.260
That's amazing.

00:04:38.260 --> 00:04:40.460
How often did you go?

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:42.270
Twice a week, I think.

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:44.550
Sometimes nights, too.

00:04:44.770 --> 00:04:47.470
Sounds like a tutoring schedule.

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:50.930
Y-Yeah, exactly! It was crazy!

00:04:52.260 --> 00:04:53.180
Ahem.

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:56.330
The secret to mixers is introducing yourself.

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:58.540
First impressions are important.

00:04:58.670 --> 00:05:01.840
An introduction that makes 
a good first impression...

00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:02.860
Got it.

00:05:03.140 --> 00:05:07.700
With today's beautiful weather, 
and my first mixer approaching, I am...

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:11.290
the green but refreshing Maki Natsuo!

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:12.690
You think you're a comedian?

00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:15.500
Comedy's too difficult for you. 
Try a normal introduction.

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:19.660
I have an older sister, so you won't 
have to marry into the family.

00:05:19.660 --> 00:05:22.960
You won't have to get involved 
in my father's business.

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:24.160
Too much!

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:26.380
You're too young to be bringing up marriage.

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:28.020
Talk about what you're good at.

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:30.040
I-I'm good at cooking.

00:05:30.040 --> 00:05:31.610
Hey, that's good.

00:05:31.610 --> 00:05:36.420
Someday I hope to learn to cook from my 
mother-in-law and master her techniques.

00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:37.900
Too much, too much, too much!

00:05:39.170 --> 00:05:40.780
Cooking's too ordinary.

00:05:40.780 --> 00:05:42.150
It doesn't make much of an impression.

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:45.700
What about you, Senpai?

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:49.300
I can stick a safety pin through my hand.

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:50.440
Enomoto 
Yuiko

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:50.450
What are you, a child?

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:51.200
What?!

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:53.280
That's amazing. How does it work?

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:54.500
Don't be impressed by this!

00:05:54.850 --> 00:05:57.710
I, Mizushima Sayori, taught her how to do it.

00:05:57.710 --> 00:05:58.920
Don't jump on the bandwagon!

00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:02.770
Suzu, why don't you try introducing yourself?

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:05.800
Who, me? Uh, um...

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:08.360
I can fold slapsticks really quickly!

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:10.420
Just how much do you like those things?

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:13.300
How would you introduce yourself?

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:13.850
What?

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:16.020
Oh, I'd like to hear that.

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:18.100
I'd like to hear that, too!

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:19.440
<i>This girl...</i>

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:22.490
Y-You newbies aren't ready to hear it yet.

00:06:22.490 --> 00:06:24.720
I'll tell you when the time is right.

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:25.940
You're dismissed for today.

00:06:25.940 --> 00:06:28.430
<b>Screwing herself over 
as much as she can</b>

00:06:28.470 --> 00:06:30.190
<b>The Next Day</b>

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:32.970
It's really coming down...

00:06:32.970 --> 00:06:33.580
What?!

00:06:34.750 --> 00:06:37.120
Riko-senpai, what do you think?

00:06:37.490 --> 00:06:40.200
Today's theme is surprising
 someone with a style change.

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:41.920
Surprising someone with bullying?

00:06:45.110 --> 00:06:48.890
I thought we could change how we 
look with simple hair arrangements.

00:06:48.890 --> 00:06:50.680
Put some more thought into it.

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:53.860
Why don't you cut that 
miserable hair of yours?

00:06:53.860 --> 00:06:57.210
Everyone's saying no boy would 
fall for you with that Sadako hair.

00:06:57.210 --> 00:06:59.060
Who's "everyone"?

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:01.840
Huh? Well, me... and Sayo...

00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:03.740
That's just two of you!

00:07:03.740 --> 00:07:05.730
No, that's everyone!

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:07.970
Well, your hair is frizzy!

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:08.380
You do see kids like that.

00:07:07.970 --> 00:07:10.570
F-Frizzy? This is called fluffy!

00:07:08.380 --> 00:07:10.570
That's your best friend you're talking about.

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:13.480
I'm letting my hair grow out for a reason.

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:17.580
Someday, I want my boyfriend 
to tell me I have pitch black hair.

00:07:17.780 --> 00:07:18.500
"Pitch black"?

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:23.720
Well, I'm growing my hair out so my boyfriend 
will tell me my hair is like cotton candy.

00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:27.840
As your childhood friend, I'm shocked 
by how stupid that revelation is.

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:30.500
Th-That's a little lame.

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:33.000
You're in no place to 
be calling anyone lame.

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:35.580
Look, I don't care about 
your pitch or candy, but...

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:36.600
It's pitch <i>black.</i>

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:37.640
It's <i>cotton</i> candy.

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:40.480
If that's all you care about, 
what does it matter if it's short?

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:42.690
What are you talking about, Riko?

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:46.280
If my hair is too short, it will 
never get tangled in his button.

00:07:46.280 --> 00:07:48.690
You still haven't given up on that plan?

00:07:49.230 --> 00:07:53.300
I won't be able to use my "Brush Your Hair 
Against His Cheek as You Pass" technique, either!

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:55.200
I think that would just annoy him.

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:57.580
You're just adding to my shock.

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:00.500
And at really high levels, 
you can even do this...

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:07.020
Letting your hair trail along the 
wall is the most important part!

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:07.860
I get it.

00:08:07.860 --> 00:08:09.630
You two are actually good friends, right?

00:08:09.890 --> 00:08:13.220
My hair is too short to use 
any of those techniques.

00:08:13.420 --> 00:08:15.420
Most people can't.

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:19.600
The most important thing is to have a 
haircut you like, that looks good on you.

00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:24.720
Love sniper Kurahashi doesn't need to 
rely on her hair to get boys, right?

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:25.530
Huh?

00:08:25.530 --> 00:08:30.130
I can become a love sniper 
like you someday, can't I?

00:08:30.260 --> 00:08:32.690
S-Sure, of course.

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:36.720
<b>Love Sniper 
Accuracy: 0%</b>

00:08:34.730 --> 00:08:36.550
What am I doing?

00:08:38.650 --> 00:08:40.700
My hair has grown, too...

00:08:45.020 --> 00:08:46.610
Kurahashi Riko-sama

00:08:46.850 --> 00:08:50.000
<i>I-Is this a l-love...</i>

00:08:51.940 --> 00:08:54.190
<i>Kurahashi-san, you're so wild.</i>

00:08:54.190 --> 00:08:57.130
<i>You're cooler and manlier than a man.</i>

00:08:57.130 --> 00:08:58.220
<i>I love you!</i>

00:08:58.520 --> 00:09:01.270
<i>Who would write this?
 It's really depressing.</i>

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:03.000
<i>I'll grow out my hair.</i>

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:05.800
<i>I'll wear some cute accessories, too!</i>

00:09:10.790 --> 00:09:12.540
That actually looks pretty good.

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:19.170
Can I help you?!

00:09:19.170 --> 00:09:21.330
You were taking a while, 
so I just came to get you.

00:09:21.590 --> 00:09:23.580
Thanks.

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:28.380
It's an emergency!

00:09:28.910 --> 00:09:29.790
What is?

00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:31.580
It's an emergency!

00:09:31.580 --> 00:09:34.130
We actually received a 
request for romantic advice.

00:09:34.420 --> 00:09:35.300
What?

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:39.490
Okay, I'm reading it.

00:09:39.670 --> 00:09:42.250
"I want to give a gift to the person I like.

00:09:42.250 --> 00:09:44.860
What should I give him?"

00:09:44.860 --> 00:09:47.730
That depends on who you're giving it to.

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:49.270
We can't answer this.

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:50.570
I'm sorry.

00:09:50.570 --> 00:09:53.080
This must have come 
because of our last meeting...

00:09:53.080 --> 00:09:55.030
It's because of what I did.

00:09:55.310 --> 00:09:57.090
I-It's all right.

00:09:57.090 --> 00:09:59.880
We have Riko-senpai to help us.

00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:00.700
That's right.

00:10:01.140 --> 00:10:05.290
Riko is familiar with all kinds of boys. 
You know what they like, don't you?

00:10:05.530 --> 00:10:06.290
Huh?

00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:16.200
Sure!

00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:18.100
I'll ask them for you!

00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:19.180
All right!

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:21.630
Please do, Master Riko.

00:10:22.330 --> 00:10:25.430
<i>She's still screwing herself over.</i>

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:29.980
<i>I don't know what boys like.</i>

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:33.570
Here's that magazine I borrowed. Thanks.

00:10:34.020 --> 00:10:35.000
Sure.

00:10:36.770 --> 00:10:37.990
This is it.

00:10:37.990 --> 00:10:39.220
<i>That's right.</i>

00:10:39.220 --> 00:10:41.410
<i>I can just gather information from magazines.</i>

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:43.830
<i>Then I can figure out what boys like.</i>

00:10:44.190 --> 00:10:45.200
Hey.

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:46.700
Kurahashi.

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:50.210
I want to know what kind 
of boys you ask for advice.

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:52.360
Could you take pictures?

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:53.900
<i>Is she a demon?</i>

00:10:55.160 --> 00:10:59.550
I'll conduct my own investigation, but
 the rest of you should ask your families.

00:10:59.550 --> 00:11:02.150
I'll ask my cousin and brother.

00:11:02.150 --> 00:11:04.430
I only have an older sister.

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:06.500
Why don't you ask your father?

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:08.210
I'm sure he'll give you a great answer.

00:11:08.210 --> 00:11:09.770
He <i>is</i> lingerie, after all.

00:11:10.710 --> 00:11:13.250
Hey, what's this about lingerie?

00:11:13.250 --> 00:11:14.860
It's nothing.

00:11:14.860 --> 00:11:20.030
Enomoto-senpai suffers from a disease 
that makes men look like lingerie.

00:11:20.480 --> 00:11:21.360
Say what?!

00:11:21.580 --> 00:11:23.990
Come on, just tell me.

00:11:23.990 --> 00:11:26.490
Otherwise I'll get some weird idea.

00:11:24.970 --> 00:11:27.290
<b>Father</b>

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:29.590
I'd like you to tell me, too.

00:11:29.590 --> 00:11:32.060
Before my imagination runs out of control.

00:11:30.730 --> 00:11:32.100
I'm going 
to work

00:11:30.730 --> 00:11:33.570
<b>Ha ha ha</b>

00:11:32.060 --> 00:11:33.580
Take it easy on her.

00:11:33.580 --> 00:11:35.290
Very well.

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:38.200
But if you laugh at all...

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:40.630
I'll cry a river.

00:11:40.980 --> 00:11:42.550
S-Sure.

00:11:40.980 --> 00:11:42.550
O-Okay.

00:11:42.570 --> 00:11:46.500
<b>Ma
Ki</b>

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:46.510
Maki's family runs the underwear 
company "True Tree."

00:11:46.510 --> 00:11:47.840
Really?

00:11:47.840 --> 00:11:48.960
That's amazing.

00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:50.520
That's a well-known brand!

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:51.560
That's it?

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:54.940
There's no reason to hide 
the lingerie thing, then.

00:11:54.940 --> 00:11:57.240
I wish that were all there was to it.

00:11:57.240 --> 00:11:58.730
Gotcha.

00:11:58.730 --> 00:12:06.130
<b>Ma
Ki</b>

00:11:58.960 --> 00:12:02.990
Also, my uncle is a television producer,

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:05.710
and he worked with True Tree 
on a certain program.

00:12:05.710 --> 00:12:07.580
This is the video.

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:09.440
Enterprise
 Documentary

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:09.440
Maki Masanobu

00:12:09.470 --> 00:12:11.860
Enterprise Documentary

00:12:14.290 --> 00:12:19.130
<b></b>President<b> Maki Masanobu</b>

00:12:14.290 --> 00:12:19.130
A certain actress said her 
body was made of wine.

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:23.800
It would seem my body
 is made of lingerie.

00:12:25.860 --> 00:12:28.950
The way he rolls his tongue on 
"-gerie" is an important point.

00:12:28.950 --> 00:12:30.560
Stop.

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:34.080
Both sleeping and awake, lingerie.

00:12:34.240 --> 00:12:37.760
My brain is shaped like a bra.

00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:43.530
My heart is a G-string.

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:45.750
"Both sleeping and awake, lingerie."

00:12:45.750 --> 00:12:48.950
Maki's father wrote the lyrics to this song.

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:51.370
<i>Why is he singing?</i>

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:54.330
Both sleeping and awake, lingerie.

00:12:54.680 --> 00:12:57.240
<i>Why are you singing, too?</i>

00:12:54.680 --> 00:12:57.990
My kidneys are lace.

00:12:58.300 --> 00:13:00.130
We're done talking about this.

00:13:00.260 --> 00:13:02.930
Anyway, let's get to our love lessons.

00:13:03.060 --> 00:13:04.930
Can I get a CD of this song?

00:13:04.930 --> 00:13:06.220
I love it.

00:13:06.220 --> 00:13:08.180
Let's start our lesson!

00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:12.220
I still haven't told them about 
"my daughter is lingerie."

00:13:13.220 --> 00:13:14.670
There's more?

00:13:14.670 --> 00:13:17.840
Have you heard of the 
"Summer Ribbon" training bras?

00:13:17.840 --> 00:13:19.520
They came out three years ago.

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:22.590
Yeah, I used those.

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:27.600
<b>Natsu

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:27.610
They went on sale just as 
she started wearing them.

00:13:27.820 --> 00:13:29.530
You're so mean!

00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:31.990
<i>I feel so conflicted.</i>

00:13:31.990 --> 00:13:35.000
How did it feel to wear Maki?

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:36.860
Don't make it sound so weird.

00:13:36.860 --> 00:13:40.270
That just means you two were 
close before you even met, right?

00:13:40.270 --> 00:13:42.140
That doesn't help!

00:13:42.140 --> 00:13:46.350
Well, they were cute and felt nice.

00:13:46.350 --> 00:13:48.030
It was a good product.

00:13:48.030 --> 00:13:51.320
Maki-senpai is great even as a bra.

00:13:51.320 --> 00:13:53.520
Please, shut up for a little bit.

00:13:55.300 --> 00:13:56.680
Cheer up.

00:13:56.680 --> 00:13:58.990
Come on, let's start Love Lab.

00:13:58.990 --> 00:13:59.700
Riko.

00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:01.690
That's right, cheer up.

00:14:01.690 --> 00:14:05.530
Kurahashi will talk to lots of boys for you.

00:14:07.420 --> 00:14:08.600
<i>I had forgotten about that.</i>

00:14:10.020 --> 00:14:12.840
<i>Should I ask the guys I went 
to elementary school with?</i>

00:14:12.840 --> 00:14:15.540
<i>I haven't seen them recently, though.</i>

00:14:15.740 --> 00:14:18.100
Riko, how'd you do on the test?

00:14:20.570 --> 00:14:22.330
Whoa, that's awful.

00:14:20.570 --> 00:14:23.970
English

00:14:22.330 --> 00:14:23.960
Though mine's pretty bad, too.

00:14:24.180 --> 00:14:26.210
Hey, do you want to go 
to cram school with me?

00:14:26.670 --> 00:14:27.620
Cram school?

00:14:27.620 --> 00:14:31.080
You know, that place you went 
to for the entrance exam.

00:14:31.080 --> 00:14:32.930
You told me about it the other day.

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:35.180
<i>I know some boys at cram school.</i>

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:36.960
I'll go with you.

00:14:36.960 --> 00:14:37.850
Really?

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:39.060
I won't attend any classes, though!

00:14:39.060 --> 00:14:40.330
Why not?

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:45.190
I'll do my investigation for romantic 
advice tomorrow after school.

00:14:45.890 --> 00:14:47.130
Really?

00:14:47.130 --> 00:14:48.460
What about my photos?

00:14:48.460 --> 00:14:50.280
Of course, I'll take some.

00:14:51.420 --> 00:14:54.630
Oh, I want to meet boys, too.

00:14:54.750 --> 00:14:56.700
Can I go with you?

00:14:56.700 --> 00:14:58.300
As if.

00:14:58.760 --> 00:14:59.880
Excuse me...

00:15:00.810 --> 00:15:04.440
Um, I'm sure I'm wrong, but...

00:15:04.700 --> 00:15:10.550
Mizushima-senpai, do you not believe 
Riko-senpai is the love sniper?

00:15:10.650 --> 00:15:11.890
<i>You ask this now?</i>

00:15:10.650 --> 00:15:11.890
Now?

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:13.720
What? Really?

00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:15.010
<i>You too?</i>

00:15:13.740 --> 00:15:15.010
You 
too?

00:15:15.380 --> 00:15:18.580
When our Love Lab was almost 
discovered the other day,

00:15:18.580 --> 00:15:21.720
I was so distraught, I couldn't do anything.

00:15:22.010 --> 00:15:25.730
But you calmly found a way 
to resolve the situation.

00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:27.400
I thought it was amazing.

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:31.160
I wished I could be strong enough 
to protect everyone just like you.

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:34.820
That's who you truly are, isn't it?

00:15:34.820 --> 00:15:38.620
You don't mistrust your 
friends or tease them, do you?

00:15:39.660 --> 00:15:41.410
Well, I...

00:15:42.430 --> 00:15:43.290
Suzu.

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:46.490
Mizushima-senpai, Riko wouldn't lie.

00:15:46.630 --> 00:15:47.850
Isn't that right?

00:15:47.850 --> 00:15:50.260
Um, y-yeah.

00:15:50.720 --> 00:15:52.060
Fine, I get it.

00:15:52.270 --> 00:15:53.760
Sorry for doubting you.

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:56.440
We're still counting on you.

00:15:56.120 --> 00:15:59.520
<b>Currently experiencing
 extreme self-loathing</b>

00:15:56.440 --> 00:15:58.230
Don't let it bother you.

00:15:58.230 --> 00:15:59.520
S-Sure.

00:15:59.880 --> 00:16:02.610
<i>That was the perfect time 
to confess and apologize.</i>

00:16:02.610 --> 00:16:04.020
<i>What an idiot.</i>

00:16:04.020 --> 00:16:13.940
Irigimi
 Cram School

00:16:04.350 --> 00:16:06.770
Hey, do you have a minute?

00:16:06.770 --> 00:16:09.450
Wow, Kurahashi, it's been a while.

00:16:09.450 --> 00:16:12.240
Could you guys help me with some stuff?

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:13.570
Sure!

00:16:14.150 --> 00:16:16.320
As promised, I asked them for you.

00:16:19.220 --> 00:16:20.590
Here's the camera.

00:16:22.630 --> 00:16:24.910
Fine. I won't say anything anymore.

00:16:24.910 --> 00:16:26.540
R-Really?

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:29.750
By the way, are these your 
ex-boyfriends and boys you've rejected?

00:16:30.020 --> 00:16:32.220
Huh? I guess...

00:16:32.480 --> 00:16:35.010
They sure look happy, though.

00:16:35.010 --> 00:16:37.680
<i>You said you wouldn't say anything anymore!</i>

00:16:35.010 --> 00:16:37.680
<b>Not thorough enough</b>

00:16:38.180 --> 00:16:41.550
Anyway, did you conduct 
