00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:54.450
What?!

00:16:54.650 --> 00:16:56.110
B-Boyfriend?!

00:16:56.320 --> 00:16:58.730
You've been going out for a while, right?

00:16:58.730 --> 00:17:00.290
Exactly six months as of yesterday.

00:17:00.540 --> 00:17:02.160
S-So long.

00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:06.210
Do you talk on the phone every 
night and go on dates every week?

00:17:06.210 --> 00:17:09.520
I think the last time I saw 
him was six months ago.

00:17:09.520 --> 00:17:12.050
You can't even call him an acquaintance, then!

00:17:12.070 --> 00:17:15.580
Boyfriend

00:17:12.070 --> 00:17:15.580
School

00:17:12.070 --> 00:17:15.580
<b>Hirosato</b>

00:17:12.070 --> 00:17:15.580
<b>Giho                                        Natsuhara</b>

00:17:12.390 --> 00:17:13.790
It's a long distance relationship.

00:17:13.790 --> 00:17:15.590
No, that's actually pretty close.

00:17:15.830 --> 00:17:18.280
Anyway, here are his answers.

00:17:18.280 --> 00:17:20.200
We email each other.

00:17:20.380 --> 00:17:22.980
"Question: How often should I answer emails?"

00:17:22.980 --> 00:17:27.420
"Answer: I don't need a reply every time. 
Once every five times would be good."

00:17:27.420 --> 00:17:29.780
"Do you want to talk for over 
ten minutes on the phone?"

00:17:29.780 --> 00:17:32.530
"If possible, I'd like you 
to call me at least once."

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:35.110
I pity your boyfriend.

00:17:35.110 --> 00:17:37.300
You're as indifferent as ever.

00:17:37.300 --> 00:17:38.150
You think so?

00:17:38.150 --> 00:17:40.640
But, if it's been six months as of yesterday,

00:17:40.640 --> 00:17:42.920
that means you remember 
the day you started dating.

00:17:42.920 --> 00:17:43.660
What?

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:47.710
You're shy like me, aren't you?

00:17:47.880 --> 00:17:49.040
No, I'm not.

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:52.000
I only remembered because 
he reminds me endlessly.

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:53.060
Really?

00:17:53.060 --> 00:17:54.170
I see.

00:17:54.700 --> 00:17:56.580
I'm not, um...

00:17:57.680 --> 00:18:01.000
<i>Suzu's kind of like Sayo's boyfriend.</i>

00:18:01.460 --> 00:18:04.480
Anyway, their answers 
couldn't be more different.

00:18:04.690 --> 00:18:07.190
They can't agree on what 
kind of gift they want.

00:18:07.480 --> 00:18:10.680
What would you most like to give a boy?

00:18:11.380 --> 00:18:14.980
I have an idea I've been sitting 
on for quite some time.

00:18:14.980 --> 00:18:17.200
I hope it hasn't been so long it's gone bad.

00:18:18.330 --> 00:18:19.570
It's a homemade—

00:18:19.570 --> 00:18:20.240
By the way...

00:18:20.830 --> 00:18:24.160
Their least favorite gift 
is something homemade.

00:18:25.280 --> 00:18:26.620
Sounds like it went bad.

00:18:26.810 --> 00:18:28.960
What's wrong with something homemade?!

00:18:28.960 --> 00:18:34.320
<b>Hat

00:18:29.360 --> 00:18:32.240
I can knit a whole outfit!

00:18:32.240 --> 00:18:34.340
You want him to wear leg warmers?

00:18:34.340 --> 00:18:38.590
I'd hate to receive something homemade 
from someone who isn't even my girlfriend.

00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:39.680
<b>Hate to receive</b>

00:18:39.910 --> 00:18:42.390
I'd use my savings to buy an expensive—

00:18:42.620 --> 00:18:44.720
Their second least favorite
 is something expensive.

00:18:45.920 --> 00:18:47.680
This one went bad, too.

00:18:47.860 --> 00:18:49.560
What's wrong with it?!

00:18:49.740 --> 00:18:53.900
It seems like you're trying to buy him 
with money, and you'll drive him away.

00:18:53.900 --> 00:18:55.010
<b>Drive him away</b>

00:18:55.250 --> 00:18:58.010
I wouldn't mind being bought, though.

00:18:58.240 --> 00:19:01.040
In fact, I'll do the buying, so give me money.

00:19:01.040 --> 00:19:02.820
What are you talking about?

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:06.510
What if we add them together and 
give them homemade money?

00:19:06.510 --> 00:19:07.700
That's a crime!

00:19:07.700 --> 00:19:10.710
I had no idea homemade 
gifts were a bad idea.

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:17.290
<b>Anguish</b>

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:13.900
Giving someone something 
I knitted was my dream.

00:19:14.040 --> 00:19:17.470
It sounds like they'd appreciate it if 
it came from a girlfriend, so go for it.

00:19:17.470 --> 00:19:18.620
Really?

00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:22.420
Then I'll make tons of clothes to 
stockpile for my future boyfriend.

00:19:18.990 --> 00:19:25.000
<b>Sparkle</b>

00:19:22.420 --> 00:19:25.010
<i>Good luck, Maki's future boyfriend.</i>

00:19:28.680 --> 00:19:30.900
I finished totaling all the results.

00:19:30.900 --> 00:19:33.310
Now, we just have to tell her the results.

00:19:33.310 --> 00:19:34.110
And...

00:19:34.350 --> 00:19:36.710
What are you doing?

00:19:37.130 --> 00:19:39.790
I'm imagining being with my future boyfriend.

00:19:39.790 --> 00:19:40.990
Okay, okay.

00:19:40.990 --> 00:19:43.840
By the way, how are we going to tell her?

00:19:43.840 --> 00:19:46.030
The question was left anonymously.

00:19:47.270 --> 00:19:51.870
Well, we could post it on a 
bulletin board or hand out flyers.

00:19:52.390 --> 00:19:54.380
Romantic relationships are forbidden.

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:56.500
We can't let the teachers find out.

00:19:56.740 --> 00:19:59.790
We could determine her identity using 
handwriting analysis and police dogs.

00:19:59.790 --> 00:20:01.930
Do we have that kind of political power?

00:20:02.220 --> 00:20:04.450
Those sound hard, so let's reply 
via a game of telephone.

00:20:04.450 --> 00:20:06.260
You can work harder than that.

00:20:06.530 --> 00:20:09.250
She must have been at the meeting that day.

00:20:09.250 --> 00:20:12.250
So we should announce the 
results at the next one.

00:20:12.250 --> 00:20:13.470
Good point.

00:20:14.270 --> 00:20:16.480
The next meeting is two months from now.

00:20:16.870 --> 00:20:18.880
Based on the request,

00:20:18.880 --> 00:20:22.220
it doesn't seem as though the object 
of her affections is her boyfriend.

00:20:22.800 --> 00:20:25.610
If her love is unrequited,

00:20:25.610 --> 00:20:29.590
it's likely she'll give a gift on an 
appropriate day, like his birthday.

00:20:30.090 --> 00:20:32.900
She asked a third party like us

00:20:32.900 --> 00:20:35.300
because she couldn't decide 
what to get him on her own.

00:20:35.730 --> 00:20:37.850
It's safe to assume she 
had been thinking about it

00:20:37.850 --> 00:20:40.590
because the day she wants to 
give him a gift is approaching.

00:20:41.060 --> 00:20:45.300
Which means it's possible that day will 
come and go in the next two months.

00:20:46.480 --> 00:20:50.580
<i>Why can't she be this calm in our Love Lab?</i>

00:20:50.580 --> 00:20:51.890
I don't care anymore!

00:20:51.890 --> 00:20:53.350
Do whatever you want!

00:20:53.350 --> 00:20:54.680
What are you talking about?

00:20:54.680 --> 00:20:56.510
We even gathered questionnaires.

00:20:56.510 --> 00:20:57.850
I don't care.

00:20:57.850 --> 00:21:01.040
Besides, this isn't the student council's job.

00:21:01.040 --> 00:21:01.610
Hey—

00:21:01.610 --> 00:21:03.400
Let's ignore it, then.

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:04.300
What?

00:21:04.300 --> 00:21:07.210
We can't ignore someone
 asking us for advice!

00:21:07.210 --> 00:21:08.230
I know, right?

00:21:08.230 --> 00:21:10.240
We need to meet her expectations.

00:21:10.460 --> 00:21:12.250
<i>She's good at handling her.</i>

00:21:14.390 --> 00:21:19.000
Enomoto-senpai, why don't we take
 a break before thinking about this?

00:21:20.470 --> 00:21:22.700
You're right. Let's do that.

00:21:22.880 --> 00:21:24.990
I'll go make some tea.

00:21:25.540 --> 00:21:26.680
I'm going to the bathroom.

00:21:29.040 --> 00:21:32.910
Enomoto-senpai, you dropped something.

00:21:32.910 --> 00:21:35.930
